      "F10": "The presence of a large, ulcerated lesion on the penis is consistent with several types of lymphoma, but the specific characteristics are more typical of aggressive lymphomas like diffuse large B-cell lymphoma.",
      "F14": "Atypical lymphocytes with CD20+, CD79a+, and CD5+ expression are more typical of B-cell lymphomas, particularly diffuse large B-cell lymphoma.",
      "F15": "Clonal IgH gene rearrangement is a hallmark of B-cell lymphomas, supporting the diagnosis of diffuse large B-cell lymphoma or mantle cell lymphoma.",
      "F16": "FDG-avid abdominal and peripancreatic lymph nodes suggest lymphoma involvement, but are not specific to any one type."
